WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.963
Everything starts with SAM.gov. Rhodo monitors federal opportunities

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:08.809
using the filters set for your firm, brings in the solicitation

00:00:08.809 --> 00:00:12.796
documents, and analyzes the work against your capabilities.

00:00:13.463 --> 00:00:17.520
So you start with relevant opportunities, and a reason to consider

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:18.488
each one.

00:00:18.615 --> 00:00:20.679
Here’s where those opportunities land.

00:00:21.134 --> 00:00:25.077
The pipeline shows what’s been analyzed, what’s moving into proposal

00:00:25.077 --> 00:00:28.487
preparation, and what’s been submitted or decided.

00:00:28.982 --> 00:00:32.085
Deadlines and fit scores help you see where to focus.

00:00:32.516 --> 00:00:35.792
Open a pursuit, and you can see the AI’s analysis.

00:00:36.228 --> 00:00:40.478
It reads the solicitation, identifies requirements, and compares

00:00:40.478 --> 00:00:43.484
them with your firm’s experience and qualifications.

00:00:44.228 --> 00:00:48.022
You get a bid recommendation, strengths, and gaps to review.

00:00:48.236 --> 00:00:52.910
That same source material grounds the AI generated proposal sections.

00:00:53.394 --> 00:00:57.433
In Selection, Rhodo recommends relevant past projects from your

00:00:57.433 --> 00:01:01.570
firm’s records. Each suggestion includes the experience supporting

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:03.845
that choice, ready for your review.

00:01:04.198 --> 00:01:07.890
It then recommends people whose qualifications and project history

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:12.351
fit the roles. You can accept the team or compare an alternative,

00:01:12.351 --> 00:01:14.973
instead of assembling the roster from scratch.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:19.307
Those choices build the experience matrix, connecting people to

00:01:19.307 --> 00:01:20.910
the projects they worked on.

00:01:21.221 --> 00:01:25.631
Your approval moves the selected team and projects into the workflow.

00:01:25.972 --> 00:01:30.472
The preparation tools generate resumes, project sheets, and supporting

00:01:30.472 --> 00:01:34.710
narratives from that material. Documents keeps the original solicitation,

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:39.133
amendments, and generated sections together, so you can check both

00:01:39.133 --> 00:01:41.159
the source and the output.

00:01:41.535 --> 00:01:46.175
The Proposal tab brings the sections into one SF330 package.

00:01:46.727 --> 00:01:50.381
Review what’s ready, address any missing information, and give

00:01:50.381 --> 00:01:52.406
it your final check before submission.

00:01:52.919 --> 00:01:55.118
And you don’t need to fix everything by hand.

00:01:55.554 --> 00:01:57.848
Tell the assistant what you want changed.

00:01:58.304 --> 00:02:02.612
Rhodo can save your feedback on tone, terminology, and how you

00:02:02.612 --> 00:02:06.573
describe your work, then use those preferences to guide future

00:02:06.573 --> 00:02:10.842
proposal drafts. Over time, that helps the writing sound more like

00:02:10.842 --> 00:02:13.713
your team, with fewer repeated corrections.

00:02:14.186 --> 00:02:19.000
Your pursue or decline decisions also help refine opportunity scoring.

00:02:19.322 --> 00:02:21.270
That’s how the workflow adapts:

00:02:21.399 --> 00:02:25.302
your firm’s knowledge and feedback carry forward, while you stay

00:02:25.302 --> 00:02:26.078
in control.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.586
Behind every pursuit is your firm’s knowledge base.

00:02:30.061 --> 00:02:32.317
Projects lets you search past work.

00:02:32.824 --> 00:02:36.009
Personnel brings together qualifications and experience.

00:02:36.888 --> 00:02:40.349
Subconsultants keeps your partner firms in view, so you can build

00:02:40.349 --> 00:02:43.105
the right team with the records you already have.

00:02:43.322 --> 00:02:47.425
The main Documents page is where new source files enter the system.

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:51.556
Upload your records, follow processing, and review information

00:02:51.556 --> 00:02:53.197
that needs clarification.

00:02:53.775 --> 00:02:56.897
Proposals gives you a view across active packages.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:01.660
Scoring Rules captures your firm’s preferences, while Metrics shows

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:04.377
pipeline activity and processing health.

00:03:04.688 --> 00:03:08.809
Help explains the workflow. Additional Folders connects supporting

00:03:08.809 --> 00:03:12.065
files, and Roadmap shows planned work.

00:03:12.401 --> 00:03:16.535
Lifecycle and Availability are marked as work in progress in this

00:03:16.535 --> 00:03:17.195
dashboard.

00:03:17.604 --> 00:03:21.969
That’s Rhodo: the monitoring, analysis, matching, and proposal

00:03:21.969 --> 00:03:26.893
preparation handled for you, with your team in control of the decisions, and

00:03:26.893 --> 00:03:29.129
support when something needs changing.
